# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
#
# crownlte (Galaxy Note9, BCM4361 PCIe) build of Samsung bcmdhd 101.16 on 6.12.
#
# Kbuild takes precedence over the 4.9 Makefile, which is kept unchanged as a
# reference. The define list below is the exact set the running 4.9 kernel
# was compiled with (crownlte 4.9 out/drivers/net/wireless/bcmdhd_101_16/
# .dhd_linux.o.cmd, including the forced -include of dhd_sec_feature.h), minus compiler/kbuild-internal macros and minus:
#   DHD_ALLOC_COHERENT_MEM_FROM_ATOMIC_POOL: non-coherent DMA on 6.12: the atomic pool is far too small for the rings
#   WL_BAM: bad-AP manager writes /data/misc/conn/ with vfs_write (stage 1: no kernel file writes)
# DHD_SUPPORT_VFS_CALL stays undefined, as on 4.9: dhd_filp_open() and the
# other dhd_vfs_* helpers are stubs, so DHD reads and writes no files.
# The object list is the 4.9 dhd.o list plus the two Exynos glue objects
# (built outside dhd.o on 4.9), minus wl_bam.o, plus the crownlte self-test.
#
# See Documentation/crownlte/wifi-port.md.

